Track 1: Ink Stung the Port-Collector
- Story & Context: At the peak of the 2028 Tilbury dock strikes, postal clerk Aris Thorne accidentally redirected a crate of custom pan drums to a derelict radar station, where he spent three foggy nights mapping their resonance against the acoustic fog-blasts of passing container ships. The local harbor master tried to shut down the makeshift studio after the low-end vibrations cracked the control tower windows, but the resulting bootleg tape had already spread through the dockworker unions. Listeners still swear the track's signature drop mirrors the precise rhythm of the vessel SS Meridian signaling her arrival through the river smog. The vocal hook echoes the tension of that intercepted shipment: "You stamped the envelope but left the harbor cold."
