Track 2: Undelivered at 4 A.M.
- Story & Context: Written in the back of a rain-slicked Ford Transit van parked outside the Thames Barrier, this track captures singer-producer Maya Lin sifting through a box of uncollected sea-mail letters left behind by merchant mariners. She picked out a mold-damaged postcard from 1994, using its forgotten address as the trigger for a pitch-shifted, future-garage vocal chop that weaves around a cavernous steel drum solo. Midway through the mix, the track cuts to total silence before a crushing big-beat snare tears through the ambient drift, simulating a sudden maritime distress call. Maya's distant, looped voice cuts through the sub-bass rumble: "I left your address written on the tide."
