Track 3: The Custom House Smudge
- Story & Context: Local legend says the master tape for this track was recorded inside an abandoned customs warehouse using a single overhead mic while two tugboats conducted a synchronized horn check in the harbor outside. Producer Slipway 9 layered those distant vessel calls underneath a cascading, space-age steel drum loop that swells into a thunderous future bass chorus. The track became the closing anthem for the scene, played at dawn as the fog finally lifted to reveal the morning freight fleets clearing the bay. The final fading bar leaves behind a single vocal refrain drifting into digital delay: "Did the envelope hold what we lost at sea?"
